The Arrays.parallelPrefix() method of the Arrays class in Java 8 is used to apply an inclusive prefix operation on an array in parallel. It performs operations like addition, multiplication, or other binary operations in parallel to speed up the processing of large arrays.Example:Below is a simple example that uses Arrays.parallelPrefix() to modify the elements of an array by performing a cumulative operation.
            Java

    import java.util.Arrays;

public class ArraysParallelPrefix {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Initial array
        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};

        // perform cumulative sum operation
        Arrays.parallelPrefix(arr, (x, y) -> x + y);

        // modified array will be printed
        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr));  
    }
}

Output[1, 3, 6, 10, 15]
Note: A cumulative operation is a process where each element in a sequence is transformed based on previous elements by updating the result across the array. It is widely used for calculations like sums, products, and even string concatenation.Table of ContentSyntax of Arrays.parallelPrefix() method Examples of Arrays.parallelPrefix() in JavaUsing Arrays.parallelPrefix() with IntBinaryOperatorDifferent Operations on Arrays Using Arrays.parallelPrefix()Using Arrays.parallelPrefix() with Custom ObjectsSyntax of Arrays.parallelPrefix() method public static void parallelPrefix(int[] array, IntBinaryOperator op)Parameters:array: Integer array on which the cumulative operation is to be performed.op: It is of type IntBinaryOperation (It represents an operation upon two int operands, and returns a result of type int).Return Type: This method does not return a value.Exception: NullPointerException: Thrown if the array or the IntBinaryOperator function passed as a parameter is null. Important Point: Arrays.parallelPrefix() supports cumulative operations on various data types like int[], double[], long[], and generic arrays (T[]) and it enables efficient parallel processing with different binary operators.Examples of Arrays.parallelPrefix() in JavaUsing Arrays.parallelPrefix() with IntBinaryOperatorIn this example, we have used the parallelPrefix() method by applying a simple addition operation on adjacent elements of an integer array. 
